        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>\"Symbol table is not required after the parsing phase.\"</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Explanation: The symbol table is essential during the </span><b><strong>lexical analysis</strong></b><span>, </span><b><strong>syntax analysis</strong></b><span>, and </span><b><strong>semantic analysis</strong></b><span> phases for storing information about identifiers, variables, functions, types, and scopes. It is used for generating the code, resolving names, checking types, and managing scopes.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>However, after the parsing phase (or semantic analysis), the symbol table is typically </span><b><strong>no longer required</strong></b><span> in many compilers, as it is not needed during the code generation or optimization phases, where the focus shifts to generating machine code.</span></p>",
