        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><br><span>To find the maximum number of bits that can be used to store the immediate operand for the given instruction, we need to analyze how the 32-bit instruction is encoded.</span></p><h3 id=\"given\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Given:</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>64 general-purpose registers</strong></b><span>: To select one of the 64 registers, we need </span><b><strong>6 bits</strong></b><span> (since 2</span><sup><span>6 </span></sup><span>= 64).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>50 distinct instruction types</strong></b><span>: To encode 50 instructions, we need </span><b><strong>6 bits</strong></b><span> (since 2</span><sup><span>6 </span></sup><span>= 64, which is enough to cover 50 instructions).</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>32-bit instruction encoding</strong></b><span>: The total size of the instruction is 32 bits.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"stepbystep-breakdown\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Step-by-step breakdown:</span></h3><ol><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Bits for the opcode (instruction type)</strong></b><span>: Since there are 50 distinct instructions, we need </span><b><strong>6 bits</strong></b><span> to encode the instruction type.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>Bits for the register operand</strong></b><span>: The instruction uses a register operand (R1 in the example). Since there are 64 registers, we need </span><b><strong>6 bits</strong></b><span> to specify a register.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>Remaining bits for the immediate operand</strong></b><span>: The remaining bits in the instruction encoding are used for the immediate operand. The total number of bits available for the immediate operand is:32 bits (total instruction size) - 6 bits (opcode) - 6 bits (register operand) = </span><b><strong>20 bits</strong></b><span>.</span></li></ol><h3 id=\"final-answer\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Final Answer:</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The maximum number of bits that can be used to store the immediate operand for the given instruction is </span><b><strong>20 bits</strong></b><span>.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So, the correct answer is </span><b><strong>20</strong></b><span>.</span></p>",
