        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>To determine which interface the packet will be forwarded to, we need to compare the destination IP address (145.36.109.70) with the subnets in the router's routing table.</span></p><h3 id=\"stepbystep-analysis\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Step-by-step Analysis:</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The destination IP address is </span><b><strong>145.36.109.70</strong></b><span>. We need to check which subnet this address belongs to based on the subnet masks in the routing table.</span></p><h4 id=\"1-first-subnet-145360016\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>1. </span><b><strong>First subnet: 145.36.0.0/16</strong></b></h4><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Subnet: </span><b><strong>145.36.0.0</strong></b><span> with a </span><b><strong>/16</strong></b><span> mask (255.255.0.0).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>This subnet includes all IPs from </span><b><strong>145.36.0.0</strong></b><span> to </span><b><strong>145.36.255.255</strong></b><span>.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>145.36.109.70</strong></b><span> falls within this range, so this is a match.</span></li></ul><h4 id=\"2-second-subnet-14536128017\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>2. </span><b><strong>Second subnet: 145.36.128.0/17</strong></b></h4><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Subnet: </span><b><strong>145.36.128.0</strong></b><span> with a </span><b><strong>/17</strong></b><span> mask (255.255.128.0).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>This subnet includes all IPs from </span><b><strong>145.36.128.0</strong></b><span> to </span><b><strong>145.36.255.255</strong></b><span>.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>145.36.109.70</strong></b><span> does </span><b><strong>not</strong></b><span> fall within this range, so it doesn't match this subnet.</span></li></ul><h4 id=\"3-third-subnet-1453664018\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>3. </span><b><strong>Third subnet: 145.36.64.0/18</strong></b></h4><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Subnet: </span><b><strong>145.36.64.0</strong></b><span> with a </span><b><strong>/18</strong></b><span> mask (255.255.192.0).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>This subnet includes all IPs from </span><b><strong>145.36.64.0</strong></b><span> to </span><b><strong>145.36.127.255</strong></b><span>.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>145.36.109.70</strong></b><span> falls within this range, so this is also a match.</span></li></ul><h4 id=\"4-fourth-subnet-14536255024\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>4. </span><b><strong>Fourth subnet: 145.36.255.0/24</strong></b></h4><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Subnet: </span><b><strong>145.36.255.0</strong></b><span> with a </span><b><strong>/24</strong></b><span> mask (255.255.255.0).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>This subnet includes all IPs from </span><b><strong>145.36.255.0</strong></b><span> to </span><b><strong>145.36.255.255</strong></b><span>.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>145.36.109.70</strong></b><span> does </span><b><strong>not</strong></b><span> fall within this range, so it doesn't match this subnet.</span></li></ul><h4 id=\"5-default-route-e5\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>5. </span><b><strong>Default route (E5)</strong></b></h4><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>If no other subnet matches, the packet will be forwarded to the default route.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"step-2-determining-the-best-match\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Step 2: Determining the Best Match</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The most specific match (longest subnet mask) for </span><b><strong>145.36.109.70</strong></b><span> is the </span><b><strong>/18</strong></b><span> subnet </span><b><strong>145.36.64.0/18</strong></b><span>, which falls within the range </span><b><strong>145.36.64.0</strong></b><span> to </span><b><strong>145.36.127.255</strong></b><span>.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Since </span><b><strong>145.36.109.70</strong></b><span> falls within this range, the packet will be forwarded to </span><b><strong>E3</strong></b><span>, which corresponds to this subnet.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"final-answer\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Final Answer:</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The packet will be forwarded to </span><b><strong>E3</strong></b><span>.</span></p>",
