        "id": 144511,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let LIST be a datatype for an implementation of linked list defined as follows:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>typedef struct list {</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-indent: 20px;\"><span>&nbsp;int data;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-indent: 20px;\"><span>&nbsp;struct list *next;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>} LIST;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Suppose a program has created two linked lists, L1 and L2, whose contents are given in the figure below (code for creating L1 and L2 is not provided here). L1 contains 9 nodes, and L2 contains 7 nodes.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider the following C program segment that modifies the list L1. The number of nodes that will be there in L1 after the execution of the code segment is ________ . (Answer in integer)</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618173106923390/two_linked_lists.png\" alt=\"two_linked_lists\" width=\"507\" height=\"83\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618173106923390/two_linked_lists.png 507w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618173106923390/two_linked_lists-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618173106923390/two_linked_lists-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618173106923390/two_linked_lists-300.png 300w\"><figcaption>Figure </figcaption></figure><pre><span>int find(int query, LIST *list) {</span><br><span>    while (list != NULL) {</span><br><span>        if (list-&gt;data == query) return 1;</span><br><span>        list = list-&gt;next;</span><br><span>    }</span><br><span>    return 0;</span><br><span>}</span><br><br><span>int main() {</span><br><span>    ... ... ...</span><br><span>    ptr1 = L1; ptr2 = L2;</span><br><br><span>    while (ptr1-&gt;next != NULL) {</span><br><span>        query = ptr1-&gt;next-&gt;data;</span><br><span>        if (find(query, L2))</span><br><span>            ptr1-&gt;next = ptr1-&gt;next-&gt;next;</span><br><span>        else</span><br><span>            ptr1 = ptr1-&gt;next;</span><br><span>    }</span><br><br><span>    ... ... ...</span><br><span>    return 0;</span><br><span>}</span><br></pre>",
