        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let's analyze the given C program to determine the value printed.</span></p><h3 id=\"c-program-breakdown\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>C Program Breakdown:</span></h3><ol><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>The function </strong></b><b><code><strong>gate(int n)</strong></code></b><span>:</span><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>This function takes an integer </span><code><span>n</span></code><span> and performs some operations on it to return a new number (</span><code><span>newnum</span></code><span>).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The variable </span><code><span>t</span></code><span> represents the place value (10's, 100's, etc.) and is used to extract the digits of </span><code><span>n</span></code><span> one by one.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>The </span><code><span>turn</span></code><span> variable controls whether we add the extracted digit (</span><code><span>d</span></code><span>) to the new number (</span><code><span>newnum</span></code><span>).</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>The digits are taken in pairs: the first digit is discarded, and the second digit is added to </span><code><span>newnum</span></code><span>.</span></li></ul></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>How it works</strong></b><span>:</span><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The </span><code><span>while (n &gt;= t)</span></code><span> loop finds the highest power of 10 (</span><code><span>t</span></code><span>) that is less than or equal to </span><code><span>n</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The next </span><code><span>while (t &gt; 0)</span></code><span> loop extracts the digits of </span><code><span>n</span></code><span> one by one.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>On each iteration, the digit </span><code><span>d</span></code><span> is extracted by </span><code><span>d = n / t</span></code><span>, and the number </span><code><span>n</span></code><span> is updated to remove the digit by </span><code><span>n = n % t</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>The digit is added to </span><code><span>newnum</span></code><span> only when </span><code><span>turn</span></code><span> is </span><code><span>1</span></code><span>, and </span><code><span>turn</span></code><span> alternates between </span><code><span>0</span></code><span> and </span><code><span>1</span></code><span>.</span></li></ul></li></ol><h3 id=\"detailed-execution-for-gate14362\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Detailed Execution for </span><code><span>gate(14362)</span></code><span>:</span></h3><ol><li value=\"1\"><span>Initially, </span><code><span>n = 14362</span></code><span>, </span><code><span>t = 1</span></code><span>, and </span><code><span>turn = 0</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The first loop </span><code><span>while (n &gt;= t)</span></code><span> is used to find the largest power of 10 less than or equal to 14362:</span><ul><li value=\"1\"><code><span>t = 10</span></code><span>, </span><code><span>t = 100</span></code><span>, </span><code><span>t = 1000</span></code><span>, </span><code><span>t = 10000</span></code><span> (stopping here because 10000 is the largest power of 10 ≤ 14362).</span></li></ul></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Now, the program begins the second </span><code><span>while (t &gt; 0)</span></code><span> loop:</span><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>First iteration</strong></b><span>: </span><ul><li value=\"1\"><code><span>d = n / t = 14362 / 10000 = 1</span></code><span> (first digit is 1).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><code><span>n = n % t = 14362 % 10000 = 4362</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><code><span>t = t / 10 = 1000</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Since </span><code><span>turn = 0</span></code><span>, the digit </span><code><span>d</span></code><span> is not added to </span><code><span>newnum</span></code><span>. </span><code><span>turn</span></code><span> changes to </span><code><span>1</span></code><span>.</span></li></ul></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>Second iteration</strong></b><span>: </span><ul><li value=\"1\"><code><span>d = n / t = 4362 / 1000 = 4</span></code><span> (second digit is 4).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><code><span>n = n % t = 4362 % 1000 = 362</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><code><span>t = t / 10 = 100</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Since </span><code><span>turn = 1</span></code><span>, </span><code><span>newnum = 10 * newnum + d = 0 * 10 + 4 = 4</span></code><span>. </span><code><span>turn</span></code><span> changes to </span><code><span>0</span></code><span>.</span></li></ul></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>Third iteration</strong></b><span>: </span><ul><li value=\"1\"><code><span>d = n / t = 362 / 100 = 3</span></code><span> (third digit is 3).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><code><span>n = n % t = 362 % 100 = 62</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><code><span>t = t / 10 = 10</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Since </span><code><span>turn = 0</span></code><span>, the digit </span><code><span>d</span></code><span> is not added to </span><code><span>newnum</span></code><span>. </span><code><span>turn</span></code><span> changes to </span><code><span>1</span></code><span>.</span></li></ul></li><li value=\"4\"><b><strong>Fourth iteration</strong></b><span>: </span><ul><li value=\"1\"><code><span>d = n / t = 62 / 10 = 6</span></code><span> (fourth digit is 6).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><code><span>n = n % t = 62 % 10 = 2</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><code><span>t = t / 10 = 1</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Since </span><code><span>turn = 1</span></code><span>, </span><code><span>newnum = 10 * newnum + d = 4 * 10 + 6 = 46</span></code><span>. </span><code><span>turn</span></code><span> changes to </span><code><span>0</span></code><span>.</span></li></ul></li><li value=\"5\"><b><strong>Fifth iteration</strong></b><span>: </span><ul><li value=\"1\"><code><span>d = n / t = 2 / 1 = 2</span></code><span> (fifth digit is 2).</span></li><li value=\"2\"><code><span>n = n % t = 2 % 1 = 0</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><code><span>t = t / 10 = 0</span></code><span>.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Since </span><code><span>turn = 0</span></code><span>, the digit </span><code><span>d</span></code><span> is not added to </span><code><span>newnum</span></code><span>. </span><code><span>turn</span></code><span> changes to </span><code><span>1</span></code><span>.</span></li></ul></li></ul></li><li value=\"4\"><span>The loop ends because </span><code><span>t = 0</span></code><span>, and the function returns </span><code><span>newnum</span></code><span>, which is </span><b><strong>46</strong></b><span>.</span></li></ol><h3 id=\"final-answer\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Final Answer:</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The value printed by the given C program is </span><b><strong>46</strong></b><span>.</span></p>",
