        "correctAnswer": 0,
        "correctAnswers": [
          0
        ],
        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>P (Unsorted doubly linked list): The meld operation for unsorted doubly linked lists involves just adjusting the pointers to connect the two lists. This can be done in constant time, Θ(1).</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Q (Min-heap): In a min-heap, meld involves combining two heaps and then reheapifying. Since the heap must maintain its properties, the worst-case time complexity is Θ(n) for merging two heaps.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>R (Binary Search Tree): For a binary search tree, melding involves merging two BSTs, which can be done by inserting all the nodes from one tree into the other. The worst-case time complexity is Θ(n), where n is the size of the tree, since each insertion could take linear time in the worst case.</span></p>",
