        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><br><span>In option (B), the schedule is conflict serializable because:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The order of transactions respects the conflict rules where one transaction's write does not interfere with the other transaction's write or read.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Transactions T1 and T2 are executed without any conflicts, meaning that if we rearrange them, the schedule can be represented in a serial order.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>In the sequence, T1 and T2's actions on the data items X and Y do not conflict with each other and can be serialized without violating any consistency rules. Hence, option B represents a conflict-serializable schedule.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2025 || CSE || MCQ"
