        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><br><span>Page size = 4096 bytes = 2</span><sup><span>12</span></sup><span> bytes, so 12 bits are needed for the offset.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Logical address space = 2</span><sup><span>32</span></sup><span> bytes, so 32 bits are required for the address.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Entries in inner page table = 4096 bytes / 8 bytes per entry = 512 entries, requiring 9 bits to index.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Total address space = b (outer page table) + 9 (inner page table) + 12 (page offset) = 32 bits.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Solve for b: b = 32 - 9 - 12 = 11.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2025 || CSE || MCQ"
