        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For outgoing packet at NAT device.</span><br><span>1. Private IP should be replaced by Public IP in the Source IP field.</span><br><span>2. ⁠Destination IP will not changed. (Decided by Source Host Only)</span><br><span>3. Header Checksum is recalculated due to modification in Source IP field.</span><br><span>4. ⁠Total Length field is remain same. (as NAT does not typically alter packet size)</span><br><br><span>Read more about </span><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/network-address-translation-nat/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>NAT.</span></a></p>",
