        "id": 14014,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let x and y be random variables, not necessarily independent, that take real values in the interval [0,1]. Let z = xy and let the mean values of x,y,z be x',y',z', respectively. Which one of the following statements is TRUE?</span></p>",
