        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>As given in the question, X and Y can take values in the interval of [0,1]. From this, we can write 0 &lt;= Y &lt;= 1.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>This can also be rewritten as 0 &lt;= XY &lt;= X.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>E(X–c) = E(X)–c where c is a constant. Also called: mathematical expectation.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Taking the expectation of the above inequality, we will get this:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>E(0) &lt;= E(XY) &lt;= E(X)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>This is also equal to 0 &lt;= E(XY) &lt;= E(X)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>This can only be true in the case when the range is specified between 0 and 1.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Therefore, the correct option is D.</span></p>",
