        "id": 13976,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider an Ethernet segment with a transmission speed of 10</span><sup><span>8</span></sup><span> bits/sec and a maximum segment length of 500 meters. If the speed of propagation of the signal in the medium is 2×10</span><sup><span>8</span></sup><span> meters/sec, then the minimum frame size (in bits) required for collision detection is</span></p>",
