        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider functions Function 1 and Function 2 expressed in pseudocode as follows:</span></p><pre><span>Function 1\t                                      Function 2</span><br><span>while n &gt; 1 do\t                                  for i = 1 to 100 ∗ n do \t</span><br><span>  for i=1 to n do</span><br><span>  x=x+1                                             x = x + 1;</span><br><span>   end for                                           end for</span><br><br><span>n = [n/2];</span><br><span>end while</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let f1(n) and f2(n) denote the number of times the statement “x = x + 1” is executed in Function 1 and Function 2, respectively.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Which of the following statements is/are TRUE?</span></p>",
