        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let U = {1, 2, 3}. Let 2U denote the powerset of U . Consider an undirected graph G whose vertex set is 2U. For any A, B ∈ 2U, (A, B) is an edge in G if and only if (i) A /= B, &nbsp;and (ii) either A Ç B or B Ç A. &nbsp;For any vertex A in G, &nbsp;the set of all possible orderings in which the vertices of G can be visited in a Breadth First Search (BFS) starting from A is denoted by B(A).</span><br><span>If ∅ denotes the empty set, then the cardinality of B(∅) is _______________</span></p>",
