        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given array, &nbsp;</span><br><span>int D[128] [128] Page frame holds 512 elements of the array D. A total 30 physical page&nbsp;</span><br><span>frames are allocated to a process that executes the following code snippet. &nbsp;</span><br><span>for (int i = 0, i &lt; 128; i++)&nbsp;</span><br><span>for (int j = 0; j &lt; 128; j++) &nbsp;</span><br><span>D[j] [i]* = 10; &nbsp;</span><br><span>for each i, the loop executes 128 times.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230804124334/Fdrawio.png\" width=\"inherit\" height=\"inherit\" loading=\"auto\"><figcaption>IMG</figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Since 30-page frames were allocated to the process. &nbsp;</span><br><span>Each physical frame holds 512 elements. &nbsp;</span><br><span>And array access is in </span><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/row-major-order-and-column-major-order/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>column-major order</span></a><span>. &nbsp;</span><br><span>D[j] [i] * = 10 &nbsp;</span><br><span>The first 4 rows belong to one page. &nbsp;</span><br><span>Since memory contains 30 page frames, and array contains 32 pages. &nbsp;</span><br><span>Page required for array = 128/4=32&nbsp;</span><br><span>No. of page fault = 128×32 = 4096</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2023 || CSE || MCQ"
