        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>f(x) and g(y) are functions of </span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">x </em></i><span>and </span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">y</em></i><span>, respectively, and </span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">f </em></i><span>(</span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">x</em></i><span>)&nbsp;= </span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">g </em></i><span>(</span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">y</em></i><span>) for all real values of x and y. Which of the following option is necessarily TRUE for all conditions?   </span><b><strong>[GATE 2023 || 2 Marks || MCQ]</strong></b></p>",
