        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Option A:</strong></b><span> It always holds because if we square the input variable, then the highest order in the polynomial will also get squared.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Option B:</strong></b><span> It is not true in cases when f(n) is a polynomial function.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Option C: </strong></b><span>An exponential function may be increasing or decreasing, so this condition may not always be true.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Option D:  </strong></b><span>Take f(n)=logn, by this example we can prove that option d is false.</span></p>",
