        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider the augmented grammar with { + , *, (, ), id } as the set of terminals.</span></p><pre><span>S</span><sup><span>`</span></sup><span> </span>[Tex]\\to[/Tex]<span>  S</span><br><span>S </span>[Tex]\\to[/Tex]<span>&nbsp; S + R | R</span><br><span>R </span>[Tex]\\to[/Tex]<span>&nbsp; R* P| P</span><br><span>P </span>[Tex]\\to[/Tex]<span>&nbsp; (S) | id</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>If I</span><sub><span>0</span></sub><span> is the set of two LR(0) items {[S` ⇢ S.], [S ⇢ S. +R]}, then </span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">goto(closure(I</em></i><i><sub><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">0</em></sub></i><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">), +)</em></i><span> contains exactly __________ items.</span></p>",
