        "id": 10391,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let R</span><sub><span>i</span></sub><span>(z) and W</span><sub><span>i</span></sub><span>(z) denote read and write operations on a data element </span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">z</em></i><span> by a transaction T</span><sub><span>i</span></sub><span>, respectively. Consider the schedule S with four transactions.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>S:</strong></b><span> R</span><sub><span>4</span></sub><span>(x)R</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span>(x)R</span><sub><span>3</span></sub><span>(x)R</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>(y)W</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>(y)W</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span>(x)W</span><sub><span>3</span></sub><span>(y)R</span><sub><span>4</span></sub><span>(y)&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Which one of the following serial schedules is conflict equivalent to S?</span></p>",
