        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given, byte-addressable primary memory of size 2</span><sup><span>32</span></sup><span> bytes = 32 bits of MM width.</span><br><br><span>Cache block size = 64 bytes = 2</span><sup><span>6</span></sup><span> bytes = 6 bits in mem block width.</span><br><br><span>Number of cache block (#lines) = Cache size / Cache block size = 32 KB / 64 bytes = 512 = 2</span><sup><span>9</span></sup><span> = 9 bits in LO.</span><br><br><span>Hence, Tag bits are = 32 - 9 - 6 = 17 bits.</span><br><br><br><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/lz3J33WzNOo?start=317\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\"></iframe></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2021 || CSE || MCQ"
