        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>This</span><b><strong> shape A</strong></b><span>  polygon \"curves inward,\" meaning it has a concave region where a line segment connecting two points might lie outside the polygon. Thus, </span><b><strong>Shape A is NOT convex</strong></b><span>.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>These</span><b><strong> shapes B, C, and D</strong></b><span>  are regular polygons or convex shapes with no inward curvature and all angles ≤180∘.</span></p><h3 id=\"so-correct-answer\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>So, correct Answer:</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>A</strong></b><span> is the shape that is </span><b><strong>NOT a convex polygon</strong></b><span>.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2021 || Set-1 || 1 Marks || MCQ"
