        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Method 1:</strong></b><span>&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Lets take |S|=1</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>S={1}</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A⊆B, and A,B are subsets of S.</span></p><table><thead></thead><tbody><tr><td><b><strong>A</strong></b></td><td><b><strong>B</strong></b></td></tr><tr><td><span>ɸ</span></td><td><span>ɸ</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>ɸ</span></td><td><span>{1}</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>{1}</span></td><td><span>{1}</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p><span>3</span><sup><span>1</span></sup><span>=3</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Lets take |S|=2</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>S={1,2}</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>P(S)= {ɸ, {1}, {2}, {1,2} }</span></p><table><thead></thead><tbody><tr><td><b><strong>A</strong></b></td><td><b><strong>B</strong></b></td></tr><tr><td><span>ɸ</span></td><td><span>ɸ</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>ɸ</span></td><td><span>{1}</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>ɸ</span></td><td><span>{2}</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>ɸ</span></td><td><span>{1,2}</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>{1}</span></td><td><span>{1}</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>{2}</span></td><td><span>{2}</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>{2}</span></td><td><span>{1,2}</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>{1,2}</span></td><td><span>{1,2}</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p><span>3</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span>=9</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>for n=3, 3</span><sup><span>3</span></sup><span>=27.</span></p><p><span>..................................</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>similarly n=4, 3</span><sup><span>10</span></sup><span>=59049.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Method 2:</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>We&nbsp;can take cases like when |A|=0, |A|=1, |A|=2 .....|A|=n, where is the cardinality of the set S.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>|A|= 0. means A=ɸ, so there will be </span><sup><span>n</span></sup><span>C</span><sub><span>0</span></sub><span> x 2</span><sup><span>n </span></sup><span>pairs of A and B.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>|A|= 1, &nbsp;there will be </span><sup><span>n</span></sup><span>C</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> x 2</span><sup><span>n-1 </span></sup><span>pairs of A and B.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>|A|= 2.&nbsp; &nbsp;there will be </span><sup><span>n</span></sup><span>C</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> x 2</span><sup><span>n-2 </span></sup><span>pairs of A and B.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Like this, when |A|=n, there will be </span><sup><span>n</span></sup><span>C</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> x 2</span><sup><span>n-n </span></sup><span>pairs of A and B.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So total pairs will be Σ</span><sup><span>n</span></sup><span>Cr x 2</span><sup><span>n-r&nbsp;</span></sup><br><span>hence after solving this... it will be come as 3</span><sup><span>n</span></sup><br><span>here n=10, so answer will be 59049.</span><br><br><span>&nbsp;</span></p>",
