        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For any mapping of vertices to real values, the shortest paths remain unchanged. All intermediate node values cancel out along any path, leaving only the source and destination node values, which add up to the path cost. Therefore, the shortest paths remain the same.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Note: Option D is incorrect due to the \"if and only if\" clause. If it were just \"if,\" the statement would be correct. The condition provided is sufficient but not necessary, making the \"only if\" part invalid. Essentially, it implies that the potential would be 0 for all vertices since they are connected to a new vertex sss with zero-weight edges. Similarly, options B and C are also incorrect for the same reason.</span></p>",
