        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let there are 'm' select lines for a </span><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/multiplexers-in-digital-logic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>multiplexer</span></a><span>, then it may have upto 2</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><sup><span>m</span></sup></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> input lines.  Given that there are 32 input lines, so there must be ⌈log</span></p><p><sub><span>2</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> (n)⌉ select lines = ⌈log</span></p><p><sub><span>2</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> (32)⌉ = 5.  Option (A) is correct.  </span></p>",
