        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>K-map for given,  </span></p><pre><span>f = Σ(0, 2, 5, 7, 8, 10, 13, 15)</span></pre><img src=\"https://cdn.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/kpmmm.png\" width=\"388\" height=\"264\" loading=\"auto\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>  Therefore, </span></p><pre><span>f = BD +B'D' </span><br><span>= (B' + D).(B + D')</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> Since all the inputs and their complements are available, so circuit implementation using NOR gate:  </span></p><img src=\"https://cdn.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/kp1-1-1.png\" width=\"352\" height=\"181\" loading=\"auto\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>  F can be implemented using </span></p><p><b><strong>3</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> NOR gates.  So, option (A) is correct. </span></p>",
