        "explanation": "<ol><li value=\"1\"><a href=\"https://\" rel=\"\"><span>Recursively enumerable languages</span></a><span> are countable. </span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Syntactically valid C program can be represented with CFG. CFG generates CFL, CFL is countable. </span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>All languages over {0, 1} may not be countable, because they may also lie in the region of 2</span><sup><span>Σ*</span></sup><span>.  </span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Set of regular languages are countable, non-regular languages may not be countable. </span></li></ol><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>  Option (C) is true.</span></p>",
