        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>According to Lagrange's theorem, states that for any finite group G, the order (number of elements) of every subgroup H of G </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>divides</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> the order of G.   Therefore, possible subgroups of group on 84 elements are : 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 12, 14, 21, 28, 42, 84.  Subgroups with element 1 and 84 are trivial groups.   The size of a largest possible </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>proper</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> subgroup of G is </span></p><p><b><strong>42</strong></b></p><p><span>.</span></p>",
