        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Recursive Enumerable Language are closed under Union, Intersection, Concatenation and Kleene Closure (but not Complementation).</span><br><span>So, we can easily rule out option (A) and option (B) comes to be TRUE.</span><br><br><span>Recursive Language are subset of REL, but option (C) is saying opposite, so Option (C) is FALSE.</span><br><span>REL are countable, since set of all Turing Machines are countable. So option (D) is also FALSE.</span><br><br><span>Only Option </span><b><strong>(B) is CORRECT</strong></b><span>.</span><br><br><br></p>",
