        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>We need a number that can be written as 20x + 7, 42y + 7, 76z + 7 for three integers x, y and z.  </span><br><span>We basically need to find least common multiple of 20 (2✕2✕5), 42(2✕3✕7) and 76(2✕2✕19) </span><br><span>which is   2✕2✕5✕3✕7✕19 = 20✕21✕19 = 420✕19 = 7980  </span><br><span>So our number is 7980 + 7 = 7987.    </span></p>",
