        "id": 8657,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let G = (V, E) be any connected undirected edge-weighted graph. The weights of the edges in E are positive any distinct. Consider the following statements:</span></p><pre><span>I. Minimum Spanning Tree of G is always unique.</span><br><span>II. Shortest path between any two vertices of G is always unique.</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Which of the above statements is/are necessarily true?</span></p>",
