        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Result of T1:</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> CA CB CC  </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Result of T2 = CR/T1</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> SA SC SD SF </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Total = 4</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> Therefore, </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>option C is correct</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Alternate Solution :</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> The output of query T1 will be the courses enrolled by student SA i.e CA , CB, CC</span><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>  The output of query T2 will be the names of the students who enrol all the courses that are the output of query T1 (</span><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/sql-division/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>division operator</span></a><span>) i.e CA, CB, CC</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> From the table we can see that SA, SC, SD, SF have enrolled all the courses so the output of T2 will have 4 rows. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>",
