        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>162 = 3 * 3 * 3 * 3 * 2</span><br><br><span>To make it a perfect cube, we need at least 2 * 2 * 3 * 3 which is 36.</span><br><br><br><br><br><br><b><strong>Alternate Solution</strong></b><span> </span><br><br><br><br><br><span>Take the prime factor of 162:</span><br><span>162 = 2 * 81 = 2 * 9 * 9 = 2 * 3 * 3 * 3 * 3, now if we add minimum two 2 and two 3, then it will be perfect cube of a number. Therefore, the value of y will be = 2 * 2 * 3 * 3 = 4 * 9 = 36</span><br><br><span>Note that you can multiple 162 with values in given options, then take cube root with the help of calculator for each option, the answer should be an integer.</span></p>",
