        "id": 3702,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider the following snippet of a C program. Assume that swap(&amp;x, &amp;y) exchanges the contents of x and y.  </span></p><pre><span>int main()</span><br><span>{</span><br><span>    int array[] = {3, 5, 1, 4, 6, 2};</span><br><span>    int done = 0;</span><br><span>    int i;</span><br><br><span>    while (done == 0)</span><br><span>    {</span><br><span>        done  = 1;</span><br><span>        for (i = 0; i &lt;= 4; i++)</span><br><span>        {</span><br><span>            if (array[i] &lt; array[i+1])</span><br><span>            {</span><br><span>                swap(&amp;array[i], &amp;array[i+1]);</span><br><span>                done = 0;</span><br><span>            }</span><br><span>        }</span><br><span>        for (i = 5; i &gt;= 1; i--)</span><br><span>        {</span><br><span>            if (array[i] &gt; array[i-1])</span><br><span>            {</span><br><span>                swap(&amp;array[i], &amp;array[i-1]);</span><br><span>                done = 0;</span><br><span>            }</span><br><span>        }</span><br><span>    }</span><br><br><span>    printf(\"%d\", array[3]);</span><br><span>}</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> The output of the program is _____.  Note: This question appeared as Numerical Answer Type.</span></p>",
