        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>g</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><sub><span>y</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>(z) = ((1-&nbsp;β)</span></p><p><b><strong> +&nbsp;</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>βz)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><sup><span>N</span></sup></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>  Expanding &nbsp;g</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><sub><span>y</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>(z) we'll get binomial distribution &nbsp;with n=N and p = β  Mean of binomial distribution is E[Y] = n*p = Nβ which seems to be the only correct option here.  Therefore, option B</span></p>",
