        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<ul><li value=\"1\"><span>static&nbsp;char var; -&gt; A variable located in data section of memory as it is static in nature</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>m = malloc(10); m = null; -&gt;This is a&nbsp;lost memory which cannot be freed as m=NULL</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Char *Ptr[10]; -&gt; 10 memory locations of char type are allocated to store addresses</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>register int var1;-&gt;&nbsp;Request to allocate a CPU register to store data</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Therefore, Option is A</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>  Refer following articles for details: </span></p><p><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/memory-layout-of-c-program/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>Memory layout of C program</span></a><span>.</span></p>",
