        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>i is integer and *p is value of a pointer to short.  1) Option 1 is wrong because we are passing \"*S\" as second argument check that S is not a pointer variable .So error 2) Second option is we are trying to store the value of f(i,s) into i but look at the function definition outside main it has no return type. It is simply void so that assignment is wrong. So error 3) Option 3 is wrong because of the same reason why option 1 is wrong 4) So option d is correct.   </span></p>",
