        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let us assume: f(1) = x. Then,</span><br><span> f(2) = f(2/2) = f(1) = x</span><br><span> f(3) = f(3+5) = f(8) = f(8/2) = f(4/2) = f(2/1) = f(1) = x</span><br><span>Similarly, f(4) = x</span><br><span>  f(5) = f(5+5) = f(10/2) = f(5) = y.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>  So it will have two values. All multiples of 5 will have value y and others will have value x. It will have 2 different values. </span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2016 || CSE || MCQ"
