        "correctAnswers": [
          2
        ],
        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Total 4. 2 J-K flip- flops for synchronous counter + 2 J-K flip-flop to make 2 bit counter. Actually, when we are repeating again then after 3 we don't know that our Synchronous counter will go to which zero. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>To make it work right, we need to move it to 1st zero after 3 2nd zero after 1 3rd zero after 2 i.e. 0 -&gt; 1 -&gt; 0 -&gt; 2 -&gt; 0 -&gt; 3 (from here it again go to 1st zero).</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> In order to decide which zero to move on we use counter from 1 to 3, I have attached truth table of normal 2 bit synchronous counter using </span><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/what-is-jk-flip-flop/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>JK flip flop</span></a><span>.  </span></p>",
