        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/gq/2016/02/2016-2-26.png\" width=\"inherit\" height=\"inherit\" loading=\"auto\"><span>&nbsp;</span><br><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><br><span>According to regular expression, automata do not accept null characters (lambda). As it says (0+1)*(0+1)(0+1)*. So here both the (0+1)* can be null. But we will still have one (0+1). So, the minimum number of states is 2. Thus, B is the correct answer.&nbsp;</span></p>",
