        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span> Given statement doesn't say that -   \"All hill-stations have a lake\" but any place having a lake is surely a hill station.  ---&gt; Ooty may or may not be a hill station      </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Hence (i) is false  ---&gt; Here, it is not a compulsion that a place need to have exactly one lake to be a hill station.      </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Hence (ii) is also false.</span></p>",
