        "correctAnswer": 2,
        "correctAnswers": [
          2
        ],
        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>To form a rectangle, we must choose two horizontal sides and two vertical sides. So, number of rectangles we can form is mC2 * nC2.  Since there are three horizontal lines, we can choose the horizontal sides in 3C2 ways. Since there are five vertical lines, we can choose the vertical sides in 5C2 ways.  The number of rectangles we can form is  = 5C2 * 3C2 = {(5*4)/2}*{(3*2)/2} = 10*3 = 30  So, option (C) is correct.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2016 || CSE || MCQ"
