        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<h3 id=\"analysis-of-the-code\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Analysis of the Code</strong></b></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The code snippet provided is an implementation of the Secant Method.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The missing part, x</span><sub><span>t</span></sub><span>​, corresponds to the intermediate value computed during each iteration.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"options-analysis\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Options Analysis</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>From the formula ​, compare the given options:</span></p><ol><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Option A</strong></b><span>:​​ </span><b><strong>Incorrect</strong></b><span> because the numerator does not match the standard formula for the secant method.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>Option B</strong></b><span>: </span><b><strong>Incorrect</strong></b><span> the formula incorrectly subtracts values related to x</span><sub><span>a</span></sub><span>​.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>Option C</strong></b><span>:</span><b><strong> Correct.</strong></b><span> This matches the standard formula for the secant method.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><b><strong>Option D</strong></b><span>: ​</span><b><strong>Incorrect</strong></b><span> The subtraction is based on xax_axa​ instead of x</span><sub><span>b</span></sub><span>​.</span></li></ol>",
