        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider alphabet ∑ = {0, 1}, the null/empty string λ and the sets of strings X</span></p><p><sub><span>0</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>, X</span></p><p><sub><span>1</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> and X</span></p><p><sub><span>2</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> generated by the corresponding non-terminals of a regular grammar. X</span></p><p><sub><span>0</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>, X</span></p><p><sub><span>1</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> and X</span></p><p><sub><span>2</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> are related as follows: </span></p><pre><span>X</span><sub><span>0</span></sub><span> = 1 X</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><br><span>X</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> = 0 X</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> + 1 X</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><br><span>X</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> = 0 X</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> + {λ} </span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> Which one of the following choices precisely represents the strings in X</span></p><p><sub><span>0</span></sub></p><p><span>?  </span></p>",
