        "id": 6801,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider the basic COCOMO model where E is the effort applied in person-months, D is the development time in chronological months, KLOC is the estimated number of delivered lines of code (in thousands) and a</span><sub><span>b</span></sub><span>, b</span><sub><span>b</span></sub><span>, c</span><sub><span>b</span></sub><span>, d</span><sub><span>b</span></sub><span> have their usual meanings. The basic COCOMO equations are of the form.</span></p>",
