        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<pre><span>S1: If a candidate is known to be corrupt, then </span><br><span>    he will not be elected.</span><br><span>S2: If a candidate is kind, he will be elected.</span><br><br><b><strong>If p → q, then ¬q → ¬p</strong></b><br><span>So from S1, </span><b><strong>elected → not corrupt</strong></b><br><span>and S2 is,   </span><b><strong>kind → elected</strong></b><br><br><span>Therefore, </span><b><strong>kind → not corrupt</strong></b><br><br></pre>",
        "tag": "GATE 2015 || CSE || MCQ"
