        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<ol><li value=\"1\"><span>In TCP, as sender and receiver can send segments at the same time, It is </span><b><strong>FULL-DUPLEX</strong></b><span>.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>TCP has options for selective acknowledgement. With selective acknowledgments </span><b><strong>(SACKs),</strong></b><span> the data receiver can inform the sender about all segments that have arrived successfully, so the sender need retransmit only the segments that have actually been lost.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>As each BYTE is counted in TCP segment, and Sequence number of First BYTE is kept into header, TCP is BYTE stream protocol.</span></li></ol><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> So, only 1</span><sup><span>st</span></sup><span>is correct and other incorrect.    &nbsp;</span></p>",
