        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The correct answer is:</span><b><strong> Females : Gynaecologist</strong></b></p><h3 id=\"explanation\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Explanation:</strong></b></h3><ol><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Understanding the relationship in the given pair:</strong></b><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>\"Children : Pediatrician\" refers to a </span><b><strong>specific group of people (children)</strong></b><span> and the </span><b><strong>specialist doctor (pediatrician)</strong></b><span> who treats them.</span></li></ul></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>Analyzing the options:</strong></b><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Adult : Orthopaedist</strong></b><span>: Incorrect. Orthopaedists specialize in bones and joints, not a specific group like \"adults.\"</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>Females : Gynaecologist</strong></b><span>: Correct. Gynaecologists specialize in treating medical issues specific to </span><b><strong>females</strong></b><span>, similar to how pediatricians specialize in children.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>Kidney : Nephrologist</strong></b><span>: Incorrect. While nephrologists specialize in kidneys, the relationship here is between an organ and a specialist, not a group of people.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><b><strong>Skin : Dermatologist</strong></b><span>: Incorrect. Similar to the kidney example, this refers to an organ/system, not a group of people.</span></li></ul></li></ol>",
        "tag": "GATE 2015 || CSE || MCQ"
