        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/slr-parser-with-examples/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>SLR Parser</span></a><span> is a type of LR parser with small parse tables and a relatively simple parser generator algorithm.  Canonical LR parser or LR(1) parser is an LR(k) parser for k=1, i.e. with a single lookahead terminal. It can handle all deterministic context-free languages.  </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/lalr-parser-with-examples/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>LALR parser</span></a><span> or Look-Ahead LR parser is a simplified version of a canonical LR parser,    </span></p><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/9LF8Bby1Qhc?start=1105\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\"></iframe>",
