        "id": 6127,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider the following grammar G. </span></p><pre><span>  S → F ⎪ H</span><br><span>  F → p ⎪ c</span><br><span>  H → d ⎪ c </span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> Where S, F and H are non-terminal symbols, p, d and c are terminal symbols. Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct? </span></p><pre><span>S1: LL(1) can parse all strings that are generated using grammar G.</span><br><span>S2: LR(1) can parse all strings that are generated using grammar G. </span></pre>",
