        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Draw the truth table of three variables and output will be 1 (true) only when exactly two variables are 1 (true) else output will be 0 (false).  Therefore, </span></p><pre><span>p    q     r   Output (f)</span><br><span>0\t0\t0\t0</span><br><span>0\t0\t1\t0</span><br><span>0\t1\t0\t0</span><br><span>0\t1\t1\t1</span><br><span>1\t0\t0\t0</span><br><span>1\t0\t1\t1</span><br><span>1\t1\t0\t1</span><br><span>1\t1\t1\t0</span><br><br></pre><pre><span>f = ( ~p ∧ q ∧ r) ∨ (p ∧ ~q ∧ r) ∨ (p ∧ q ∧ ~r)</span><br><span>f = {( ~p ∧ q ) ∨ (p ∧ ~q )} ∧ r  ∨ (p ∧ q ∧ ~r)</span><br><span>f = {(p ⊕ q )} ∧ r  ∨ (p ∧ q ∧ ~r)</span><br><span>f = {~ (p ↔ q )} ∧ r  ∨ (p ∧ q ∧ ~r)</span><br></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> Hence, option (b) is true.   </span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2014 || CSE || MCQ"
