        "id": 7408,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider a hash table with 9 slots. The hash function is </span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">ℎ(k) = k mod 9</em></i><span>. The collisions are resolved by chaining. The following 9 keys are inserted in the order: 5, 28, 19, 15, 20, 33, 12, 17, 10. The maximum, minimum, and average chain lengths in the hash table, respectively, are</span><br></p>",
