        "correctAnswers": [
          0
        ],
        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<pre><span> T(n) = 2T(n/2) + log n</span><br><span> T(1) = 1</span><br><span>Substitute n = 2^k</span><br><br><span>T(2^k)  = k + 2T(2^(k-1))</span><br><span>T(2^k)  = k + 2(k-1) + 4T(2^(k-2))</span><br><span>        = k + 2(k-1) + 4(K-2) + 8T(2^(k-3))</span><br><span>        = k + 2(k-1) + 4(K-2) + 8(k-3) + 16T(2^(k-4))</span><br><span>        = k + 2(k-1) + 4(K-2) + 8(k-3) + ...... + 2^kT(2^(k-k))</span><br><span>        = k + 2(k-1) + 4(K-2) + 8(k-3) + .......+ 2^kT(1)</span><br><span>        = k + 2(k-1) + 4(K-2) + 8(k-3) + .......+ 2^k  --------(1)</span><br><br><span>2T(2^k) =     2k     + 4(k-1) + 8(K-2) + ...... + 2*2^k + 2^(k+1) --------(2)</span><br><br><span>Subtracting 1 from 2, we get below</span><br><span>T(2^k) = - k + 2 + 4 ......    2^(k-2) + 2^(k-1) + 2^k + 2^(k+1)</span><br><span>           = - k + 2 * (1 + 2 + 4 + ..... 2^k)</span><br><span>           = -k + [2*(2^k - 1)] / [2-1]</span><br><span>           = -k + [2*(2^k - 1)]</span><br><br><span>T(n) = -Logn + 2*(n - 1)</span><br><br><span>T(n)  = Θ(n) </span><br></pre>",
        "tag": "GATE 2014 || CSE || MCQ"
