        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<pre><span>Total ways to pick 4 computers = 10*9*8*7</span><br><br><span>Total ways that at least three computers are fine = </span><br><span>        Total ways that all 4 are fine + Total ways any 3 are fine</span><br><br><span>Total ways that all 4 are fine = 4*3*2*1</span><br><br><span>Total ways three are fine = 1st is Not working and other 3 working + </span><br><span>                            2nd is Not working and other 3 working + </span><br><span>                            3rd is Not working and other 3 working + </span><br><span>                            4th is Not working and other 3 working + </span><br><span>                         = 6*4*3*2 + 4*6*3*2 + 4*3*6*2 + 4*3*2*6</span><br><span>                         = 6*4*3*2*4</span><br><br><br><span>The probability = Total ways that at least three computers are fine /  </span><br><span>                  Total ways to pick 4 computers </span><br><span>                =  (4*3*2*1 + 6*4*3*2*4) / (10*9*8*7)</span><br><span>                = (4*3*2*25) / (10*9*8*7)</span><br><span>                = 11.9% </span></pre>",
