        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>There are finite number of strings of length ‘2014’. So, a turing machine will take the input string of length ‘2014’ and test it.</span><br><br><span>If, input string is present in the language then turing machine will halt in final state .</span><br><br><span>But, if turing machine is unable to accept the input string then it will halt in non-final state or go in an infinite loop and never halt.</span><br><span>Thus, ‘L’ is undecidable and recursively enumerable.</span><br><br><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/KrtQIYMB_PY?start=1846\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\"></iframe><br><br><span>Please comment below if you find anything wrong in the above post.</span></p>",
