        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>First, note that V1+V2 is still in V, so dim(V1+V2)≤ 6. We know that dim(V1+V2)=dimV1+dimV2−dim(V1∩V2). So 6≥dim(V1+V2)=dimV1+dimV2−dim(V1∩V2) dim(V1∩V2)≥4+4−6=2. </span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2014 || CSE || MCQ"
