        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let x = {a, b, c} and y = {1, 2}</span><br><span>A Function f maps each element of x to 1 in y.</span><br><span>f(a)=1 , f(b)=1 , f(c) =1</span><br><span>A = {a, b} B = {b, c}</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Option:</strong></b><span> For any subsets A and B of X, | f (A ∪ B) | = | f(A) | + | f(B) |</span><br><span>| f(A ∪ B) | = |f({a, b, c})| = 3</span><br><span>| f(A)|+|f(B)| = 2 + 2 = 4 , LHS != RHS.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Option:</strong></b><span> For any subsets A and B of X, f (A ∩ B) = f(A) ∩ f(B)</span><br><span>f(A ∩ B) = f({b}) = { 1 }</span><br><span>f(A) ∩ f(B) = {1, 1} ∩ {1, 1} = {1, 1}</span><br><span>LHS != RHS</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Option:</strong></b><span> For any subsets A and B of X, | f (A ∩ B) | = min { | f(A) |, | f(B) | }</span><br><span>|f(A ∩ B)| = |f({b})| = |{ 1 }| = 1</span><br><span>min{|f(A)|,|f(B)|} = min(2,2) = 2</span><br><span>LHS != RHS</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Option:</strong></b><span> For any subsets S and T of Y, f</span><sup><span>-1</span></sup><span> (S ∩ T) = f</span><sup><span>-1</span></sup><span> (S) ∩ f</span><sup><span>-1</span></sup><span> (T)</span><br><span>In a function a value can be mapped only to one value.</span></p>",
