        "explanation": "<pre><span>Number of female students in 2011 and 2012 are equal.</span><br><span>Suppose they are x.</span><br><br><span>Now,</span><br><span>Males students in 2011 = Female students in 2011 </span><br><span>                       = x (as the ratio is 1)</span><br><br><span>And in 2012, Male students / Female students = </span><br><span>                                       1.5(Given)</span><br><br><span>Hence Male students in 2012 = 1.5 * Female students </span><br><span>                            = 1.5 * x</span><br><br><span>Now ratio of Male students in 2012 to Male students</span><br><span>in 2011 = ( 1.5 * x ) / x</span><br><span>        = 1.5 / 1</span><br><span>i.e. 1.5 : 1</span><br><br><span>Hence C is the answer. </span></pre>",
