        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider the set of strings on {0,1} in which, every substring of 3 symbols has at most two zeros. For example, 001110 and 011001 are in the language, but 100010 is not. All strings of length less than 3 are also in the language. A partially completed DFA that accepts this language is shown below.&nbsp;</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230118010204/Capture.JPG\" width=\"712\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230118010204/Capture.JPG 712w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230118010204/Capture-100.JPG 100w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230118010204/Capture-200.JPG 200w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230118010204/Capture-300.JPG 300w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230118010204/Capture-660.JPG 660w, \" loading=\"auto\"><figcaption>&nbsp;</figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>&nbsp;The missing arcs in the DFA are&nbsp;</span></p>",
