        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>1.Certainly! To provide a solution, let's revisit the code and break down the execution:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>2. Global Variables: `a`, `b`, and `c` are declared with `c` initialized to 0.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>3. Function Declaration: `prtFun` is declared.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>4. Main Function Execution:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - A static local variable `a` is declared and initialized to 1.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - `prtFun` is called.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - `prtFun`'s static local variable `a` is initialized to 2.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - A local variable `b` is declared and initialized to 1.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - `a` in `prtFun` is incremented by `++b`, resulting in `a = 4` and `b = 2`.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - Values of `a` and `b` are printed from `prtFun`.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - `a` in `main` is incremented by 1, making it 2.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - `prtFun` is called again.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - `a` in `prtFun` is now 4 (the static variable retains its value), and `b` is 1.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - `a` in `prtFun` is incremented by `++b`, resulting in `a = 6` and `b = 2`.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>   - Values of `a` and `b` are printed again from `prtFun`.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>5. Final Print in Main**: Prints the values of `a` (2) and the global `b` (0).</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><p><span>4 2 </span></p><p><span>6 2 </span></p><p><span>2 0</span></p>",
