        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>There is no break statement in case ‘A’. If a case is executed and it doesn’t contain break, then all the subsequent cases are executed until a break statement is found. That is why everything inside the switch is printed. Try following program as an exercise. </span></p><pre><span>int main()</span><br><span>{</span><br><span>    char inchar = 'A';</span><br><span>    switch (inchar)</span><br><span>    {</span><br><span>    case 'A' :</span><br><span>        printf (\"choice A \\n\") ;</span><br><span>    case 'B' :</span><br><span>    {</span><br><span>        printf (\"choice B\") ;</span><br><span>        break;</span><br><span>    }</span><br><span>    case 'C' :</span><br><span>    case 'D' :</span><br><span>    case 'E' :</span><br><span>    default:</span><br><span>        printf (\"No Choice\") ;</span><br><span>    }</span><br><span>}</span></pre>",
