        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Total possible number of functions is 2</span><sup><span>n</span></sup><span>.&nbsp;</span><br><br><span>In mathematics, a function f from a set X to a set Y is surjective (or onto), or a surjection, if every element y in Y has a corresponding element x in X such that f(x) = y</span><br><br><span>There are total 2 functions out of 2</span><sup><span>n</span></sup><span> that are NOT onto: one that maps to all 1s and other that maps to all 2s.&nbsp;</span><br><br><span>Therefore total number of onto functions is 2</span><sup><span>n</span></sup><span> - 2.&nbsp;</span></p>",
