        "id": 4823,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A deterministic finite automation (DFA)D with alphabet&nbsp;{a,b} is given below</span><br><br><img src=\"http://www.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/gq/2013/12/GATE2011AT1.png\" alt=\"GATE2011AT1\" width=\"386\" height=\"165\" loading=\"auto\"><br><br><span>Which of the following finite state machines is a valid minimal DFA which accepts the same language as D?</span><br><br><img src=\"http://www.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/gq/2013/12/GATE2011AT2.png\" alt=\"GATE2011AT2\" width=\"562\" height=\"167\" loading=\"auto\"><br><img src=\"http://www.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/gq/2013/12/GATE2011AT3.png\" alt=\"GATE2011AT3\" width=\"578\" height=\"178\" loading=\"auto\"></p>",
