        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>We have t flip flop Truth table of t flip flop &nbsp;</span></p><table><thead></thead><tbody><tr><td><span>t</span></td><td><span>q</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>q</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>q’</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So q0 always inverted as t=1 always So 1)q10=1 2)q0 =0 3)q0 =1 4)q0 =1 For q1 also t=1 always but clock is so we have to observe positive edge of clock I.e. when is q0 going from 0 -&gt; 1 1)q1 =1 2)q1 =1 3)q1 =0 4)q1 =0 So final combination q0q1-&gt;(11,10,01,00) Ans (A)</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE 2010 || CSE || MCQ"
