        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Array: [1,&nbsp;3,&nbsp;5,&nbsp;7,&nbsp;9,&nbsp;11,&nbsp;x,&nbsp;15,&nbsp;13]</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Insertion sort makes 1 swap to place 13 before 15.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So,𝑥 must cause exactly 1 more swap.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Try values of 𝑥 that are just slightly out of order.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>When:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>x=10: swaps with 11 → 1 swap</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>x=14: 13 (later) swaps with 15 and 14 → 1 more swap</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Total = 2 swaps.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> Final Answer:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>                𝑥=10   or 14 </span></p>",
