        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>since </span>[Tex]Y = Z^2\r\n\r\n[/Tex]<span> where Z∼N(0,1) Y follows a chi-square distribution with 1 degree of freedom, denoted  </span>[Tex]\\chi^2_1\r\n[/Tex]<span> For a chi-square distribution with k degrees of freedom:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>              E[Y]=k</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>              var[y] = 2k </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>    here, with k = 1; </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>                           Var[y] = 2.1 = 2 </span></p>",
