        "correctAnswers": [
          2
        ],
        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Start at S.</strong></b></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Expand </span><b><strong>A</strong></b><span> next because it has the lowest fff-value among the frontier nodes.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Then </span><b><strong>C</strong></b><span> comes out (next lowest fff), and its successors are added.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><b><strong>B</strong></b><span> is expanded before </span><b><strong>D</strong></b><span>, again due to lower fff, tie‑broke alphabetically.</span></li><li value=\"5\"><span>Then </span><b><strong>D</strong></b><span>, and finally </span><b><strong>G</strong></b><span> is reached and expanded.</span></li><li value=\"6\"><span>Once </span><b><strong>G</strong></b><span> (the goal) is popped from the priority queue, the search terminates.</span></li><li value=\"7\"><span>In total: </span><b><strong>S, A, C, B, D, G</strong></b><span>.</span></li></ul>",
        "tag": "GATE 2025 || DA || MCQ"
