        "questionType": "MSQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Preorder + Inorder (Option A): Preorder identifies the root nodes, and Inorder specifies the left and right subtrees. Together, they uniquely reconstruct the tree.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Inorder + Postorder (Option B)</span><b><strong>:</strong></b><span> Postorder identifies the root nodes in reverse, and Inorder specifies the subtrees. This combination also uniquely reconstructs the tree.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Preorder + Postorder (Option C): For full binary trees, Preorder and Postorder can uniquely reconstruct the tree, as every internal node in a full binary tree has exactly two children.</span></p>",
