        "id": 78421,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Euclidean distance-based k-means clustering algorithm was run on a dataset of 100 points with k=3. If the points </span>[Tex]\\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\text{ and } \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}[/Tex]<span> are both part of cluster 3, then which one of the following points is necessarily also part of cluster 3?</span></p>",
