        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>In \\alpha-\\beta pruning, m represents the best value for the MAX player and is initialized to -\\infty, while n represents the best value for the MIN player and is initialized to +\\infty.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>During the search, m updates to the highest value for MAX, and n updates to the lowest value for MIN. Thus, the correct choice is m=highest, n=lowest.</span></p>",
