        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A simplified small-signal equivalent circuit of a BJT-based amplifier is given  below.   The small-signal voltage gain V</span><sub><span>o</span></sub><span>/V</span><sub><span>s</span></sub><span> (in V/V) is ___________. </span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618131601525045/GATE-ECE-2025-Q21.webp\" alt=\"GATE-ECE-2025-Q21\" width=\"631\" height=\"308\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618131601525045/GATE-ECE-2025-Q21.webp 631w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618131601525045/GATE-ECE-2025-Q21-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618131601525045/GATE-ECE-2025-Q21-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250618131601525045/GATE-ECE-2025-Q21-300.webp 300w\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p><br></p>",
        "options": [
          "<p>[Tex]\\frac{-\\beta R_L}{R_S+R_\\pi} [/Tex]</p>",
          "<p>[Tex]\\frac{+\\beta R_L}{R_S}[/Tex]</p>",
          "<p>[Tex]\\frac{-\\beta R_L}{R_S}[/Tex]</p>",
          "<p>[Tex]\\frac{+\\beta R_L}{R_S+r_\\pi}[/Tex]</p>"
        ],
        "correctAnswer": 0,
