        "questionType": "MSQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>When the message signal m(t) remains strictly positive over time, an envelope detector is suitable for demodulating a DSB-SC signal. On the other hand, for AM signals, envelope detection is still effective even if m(t) takes on negative values</span></p>",
