        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>We are provided with the following parameters:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Number of bits per sample:</strong></b><span> </span>[Tex]n = 10[/Tex]</li><li value=\"2\"><span>Sampling rate: </span>[Tex]f_s = 1\\, \\text{MHz}\r\n[/Tex]</li><li value=\"3\"><span>Maximum (full-scale) voltage: </span>[Tex]\\text{Full scale voltage} = 3.3\\, \\text{V}\r\n[/Tex]</li><li value=\"4\"><span>Message signal frequency:  </span>[Tex]f_m = 500\\, \\text{kHz}\r\n[/Tex]</li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> </span><b><strong>Signal-to-Noise Ratio (SNR)</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The theoretical SNR for an nnn-bit ADC is given by:</span></p><p>[Tex]\\text{SNR (dB)} = 1.76 + 6.02 \\cdot n\r\n[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Substituting the value of n=10:</span></p><p>[Tex]\\text{SNR} = 1.76 + 6.02 \\times 10 = 61.96\\, \\text{dB}\r\n[/Tex]</p><h3 id=\"bit-rate-calculation\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Bit Rate Calculation</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The bit rate of the system is calculated as:</span></p><p>[Tex]R_b = n \\cdot f_s = 10 \\cdot 1\\, \\text{MHz} = 10\\, \\text{Mbps}\r\n[/Tex]</p>",
