        "id": 157447,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The intrinsic carrier concentration of a semiconductor is 2.5×10</span><sup><span>16</span></sup><span> /m</span><sup><span>3</span></sup><span> at 300 K.   If the electron and hole mobilities are 0.15 m</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span>/Vs and 0.05 m</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span>/Vs, respectively, then  the intrinsic resistivity of the semiconductor (in kΩ.m) at 300 K is ________.   (Charge of an electron 𝑒 = 1.6×10</span><sup><span>−19</span></sup><span> C.)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>",
