        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given: AOI (AND-OR-Invert) gate</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1: </strong></b><span>Understand the circuit</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Top AND: </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A.B = AB</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Bottom AND has floating inputs</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>In TTL logic:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Floating input = 1</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So, 1 . 1 = 1</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2: </strong></b><span>OR operation</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>AB + 1</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Using identity:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>X + 1 = 1</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So,</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>AB + 1 = 1</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> Inversion (AOI)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\">[Tex]Y = \\overline{1} = 0[/Tex]</p>",
