        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>f (0, 0) = f (0,1) = f (1, 1) = 1; f (1, 0) = 0</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So the function is:</span></p><p>[Tex]f = \\overline{x} + y[/Tex]</p><p><span>Since complements are not directly available, implement </span>[Tex]\\overline{x}[/Tex]<span> using a NOR gate:</span></p><p>[Tex]\\overline{x} = x \\downarrow x[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Now,</span></p><p>[Tex]f = (x \\downarrow x) + y[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Thus, required gates:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>1 NOR gate (to generate </span>[Tex]\\overline{x}[/Tex]<span>)</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>1 OR gate</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Total cost = 2 units</span></p>",
