        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> Analyze the First 2:1 MUX (Left)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The characteristic equation for a 2:1 MUX is Y = S̄ I₀ + S I₁</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Inputs: I₀ = C, I₁ = C̄</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Select Line (S): B</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Output (E): E = B̅C + BC̅ (This is B ⊕ C)  </span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Analyze the Second 2:1 MUX (Right)</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Inputs: I₀ = 0, I₁ = A</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Select Line (S): E (Output of the first MUX)</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Output (f): f = E̅(0) + EA = AE</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> Substitution and Final Expression</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Substitute the value of E from Step 1 into the expression for f:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>f = A(B̅C + BC̅)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>f = AB̅C + ABC̅</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
