        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A half-subtractor requires two outputs: Difference (D = X ⊕ Y) and Borrow (B = X̅Y).</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Using the 2:1 MUX characteristic equation Y = S̄ I₀ + S I₁, the circuit implements this logic as follows:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>1. Difference (D): With select line S = X and inputs I₀ = Y, I₁ = Ȳ, the output is</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>-&gt; D = X̅Y + XY̅</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>2. Borrow (B): With select line S = X and inputs I₀ = Y, I₁ = 0, the output is</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>-&gt; B = X̅Y + X·0 = X̅Y</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Since both outputs correctly match the Boolean functions of a half-subtractor, this configuration is the correct implementation.</span></p>",
