        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>The 2:4 decoder activates only one output line based on select inputs C₁ C₀</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Each decoder output enables a corresponding tristate buffer, allowing only one input (P, Q, R, or S) to pass to output Y:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>C₁ C₀ = 00 → Y = P</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>C₁ C₀ = 01 → Y = Q</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>C₁ C₀ = 10 → Y = R</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>C₁ C₀ = 11 → Y = S</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Thus, one of four inputs is selected based on control lines.</span></p>",
