        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>A Master-Slave flip-flop consists of two latches connected in series. The Master responds to the input while the clock is high, but the Slave (and therefore the final output) only updates when the clock transitions. Since the final output is taken from the Slave, the output only changes when the state of the slave is affected.</span></p>",
