        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For D flip-flops, the next state simply takes the value of the D input. From the diagram:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>D₁ = Q₀</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>D₀ = (Q₁ + Q₀)̅ (due to the NOR gate)</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>State Trace:</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Starting from Q₁Q₀ = 00:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>• Current 00: D₁ = 0, D₀ = (0 + 0)̅ = 1 → Next state is 01.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>• Current 01: D₁ = 1, D₀ = (0 + 1)̅ = 0 → Next state is 10.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>• Current 10: D₁ = 0, D₀ = (1 + 0)̅ = 0 → Next state is 00.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The sequence loops back to the start: 00, 01, 10, 00, 01.</span></p>",
