        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>There are two latches:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>1. NAND Latch</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Works with active LOW inputs</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Initial input: (0,1) → forces outputs to (1,0)</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Then input becomes (1,1) → latch holds previous state</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Final output: (1,0)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>2. NOR Latch</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Works with active HIGH inputs</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Initial input: (0,1) → forces outputs to (1,0)</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Then input becomes (1,1) → this is invalid condition</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>But due to previous state, it settles to (0,0)</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Final output: (0,0)</span></p>",
