        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>From the circuit diagram, the inputs to the JK flip-flops are:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>J₁ = Q̅₂, K₁ = Q₂</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>J₂ = Q₁, K₂ = Q̅₁</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Since K is the exact complement of J for both flip-flops, they behave identically to D flip-flops. The next state simply takes the value of the J input. Therefore, the next state equations are:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Q₁(n+1) = Q̅₂</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Q₂(n+1) = Q₁</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Using these equations, we can trace the state transitions starting from the initial state of 0,0:</span></p><table><thead><tr><th><span>Clock Pulse</span></th><th><span>Current State (Q1, Q2)</span></th><th><span>Next State (Q1, Q2)</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span>Initial</span></td><td><span>0, 0</span></td><td><span>1, 0</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>1st</span></td><td><span>1, 0</span></td><td><span>1, 1</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>2nd</span></td><td><span>1, 1</span></td><td><span>0, 1</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>3rd</span></td><td><span>0, 1</span></td><td><span>0, 0</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>4th</span></td><td><span>0, 0</span></td><td><span>1, 0 (repeats)</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Reading the values generated specifically at Q₁ starting from the initial state, the sequence is </span><b><strong>01100</strong></b></p>",
