        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tThe figure shows a binary counter with synchronous clear input. With the decoding logic shown, the counter works as a</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2025-09-22-163316\" height=\"206\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250922163232379100/Screenshot-2025-09-22-163316.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250922163232379100/Screenshot-2025-09-22-163316.png 267w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250922163232379100/Screenshot-2025-09-22-163316-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250922163232379100/Screenshot-2025-09-22-163316-200.png 200w\" width=\"267\"/><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><br/><span>(</span><b><strong>GATE 2015</strong></b><span> ||  EC || MCQ || 1 MARK)</span></p>",
