        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Logic Gate: </strong></b><span>The clear input C̅L̅R̅ is active-low and connected to an XNOR gate with inputs Q₃ and Q₂ .</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Clear Condition:</strong></b><span> An XNOR gate outputs 0 only when its inputs are different. So, the counter will clear when Q₃ ≠ Q₂.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>State Trace:</strong></b></p><table><thead><tr><th><span>State (Decimal)</span></th><th><span>Q3</span></th><th><span>Q2</span></th><th><span>CLR (Clear)</span></th><th><span>Operation</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span>0000 (0)</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>Counts normally</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>0001 (1)</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>Counts normally</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>0010 (2)</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>Counts normally</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>0011 (3)</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>Counts normally</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>0100 (4)</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>Clear activates</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Synchronous Clear Concept: </strong></b><span>Because the clear is synchronous, the counter does not reset instantly. It stays in state 4 for the entire clock cycle and resets to 0 strictly on the next clock edge.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The counter goes through 5 distinct states (0,1,2,3,4) before resetting. Therefore, it is a Mod-5 counter.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
