        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>Clock frequency = 1 GHz -&gt; clock period = 1 ns</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The NAND gate has a delay of 2 ns. If there were no delay, the counter would reset at count 6 -&gt; mod-6 counter.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>However, due to 2 ns delay, the reset signal is delayed by 2 clock cycles. During this delay, the counter advances two additional states.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Thus, instead of resetting at 6, it continues counting up to 8 states.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
