        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The circuit has 3 D flip-flops connected in a feedback loop through an XOR gate, which makes it behave like a linear feedback shift register (LFSR).</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Initial state is 000</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The XOR feedback (from Q₁ and Q₂) generates new bits and shifts them through the flip-flops at each clock edge</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>This creates a pseudo-random sequence of states</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Starting from 000 and applying the feedback logic, the sequence progresses through different states, and after 5 clock edges, the state becomes 100</span><br/></p>",
