        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The input clock is 12 kHz</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The circuit has two D flip-flops connected in sequence</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Each flip-flop divides the frequency by 2:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>After first flip-flop → 12 / 2 = 6 kHz</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>After second flip-flop → 6 / 2 = 3 kHz</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>But due to the feedback logic (AND gate), the circuit behaves like a mod-3 counter, not a simple divide-by-4.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So effective division:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>12 kHz÷3=4 kHz</span></p>",
