        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>The gain must be adjustable in 100 increments, which means we need to represent 100 distinct levels.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>In digital systems, the number of levels that can be represented using n bits is:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>2</span><sup><span>n</span></sup></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>We need the smallest n such that:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>2</span><sup><span>n</span></sup><span> ≥ 100</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Checking:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>2</span><sup><span>6</span></sup><span> = 64 not enough</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>2</span><sup><span>7</span></sup><span> = 128 sufficient</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So, 7 bits are required to represent at least 100 levels.</span></p>",
