        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>In the following circuit, the comparator output is logic \"1\" if V</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> &gt; V</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> and logic \"0\" otherwise. The D/A conversion is done as per the relation:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>V</span><sub><span>DAC</span></sub><span> = Σ(2</span><sup><span>(n−1)</span></sup><span> b</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span>) Volts</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>where b</span><sub><span>3</span></sub><span> (MSB), b</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span>, b</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>, and b</span><sub><span>0</span></sub><span> (LSB) are the counter outputs. The counter starts from the clear state. </span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"2056957909\" height=\"400\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260505115205795463/2056957909.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260505115205795463/2056957909.webp 725w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260505115205795463/2056957909-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260505115205795463/2056957909-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260505115205795463/2056957909-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260505115205795463/2056957909-660.webp 660w\" width=\"725\"/><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The stable reading of the LED display is </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>(</span><b><strong>GATE 2008 </strong></b><span>|| EC || MCQ || 1 MARK)</span></p>",
