        "correctAnswer": 0,
        "correctAnswers": [
          0
        ],
        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For an n-bit ADC, the maximum SNR is given by:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>SNR=6.02n+1.76 dB</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For n = 10:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>SNR=6.02×10+1.76=61.96 dB</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The data rate depends on:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Number of bits per sample = 10 bits</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Sampling frequency = 1 MHz</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Data rate=10×1 MHz=10 Mbps</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>(The input frequency 500 kHz just satisfies Nyquist, no effect on data rate)</span></p>",
