        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given the clock frequency f = 1 GHz, the clock period is T = 1 / f = 1 ns.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Throughput: </strong></b><span>The circuit acts as a shift register, meaning it outputs exactly 1 bit every clock cycle.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Throughput = 1 bit / 1 ns = 1,000,000,000 bits/s = 1000 Mbits/s.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Latency: </strong></b><span>Latency is the time it takes for a single input bit to reach the final output. Because it must propagate through 3 flip-flops in series, it takes 3 full clock cycles.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Latency = 3 × 1 ns = 3 ns.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
