        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>From the given circuit diagram, we can determine the Boolean equations for the T flip-flop inputs by tracing the connections to the OR gates:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>T₁ = Q₀ + Q̅₁ (The left OR gate receives Q₀ from the top feedback wire and Q̅₁ from the first flip-flop.)</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>T₀ = Q₁ + Q₀  (The right OR gate receives Q₁ from the first flip-flop and Q₀ from the top feedback wire.)</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For a T flip-flop, the output toggles if T = 1 For a T flip-flop, the output toggles if T = 0. Starting from the initial state of 00, we can trace the sequence:</span></p><table><thead><tr><th><span>Present State (Q₁ Q₀)</span></th><th><span>T₁ = Q₀ + Q̅₁</span></th><th><span>T₀ = Q₁ + Q₀</span></th><th><span>Next State (Q₁⁺ Q₀⁺)</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span>00</span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>10</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>10</span></td><td><span>0</span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>11</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>11</span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>00</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Therefore, final sequence is 00→10→11→00</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
