        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Conductivity of intrinsic silicon sample is defined as, σ = q(N</span><sub><span>d</span></sub><span>μ</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> + N</span><sub><span>a</span></sub><span>μ</span><sub><span>p</span></sub><span>)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For n-type silicon sample, N</span><sub><span>d</span></sub><span> &gt;&gt; N</span><sub><span>a</span></sub><span> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Then, σ ≈ qN</span><sub><span>d</span></sub><span>μ</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Ratio = (qN</span><sub><span>d</span></sub><span>μ</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span>) / (qn</span><sub><span>i </span></sub><span>(μ</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> + μ</span><sub><span>p</span></sub><span>)) = (Ndμ</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span>) / (n</span><sub><span>i </span></sub><span>(μ</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> + 0.4μ</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span>))   (given, μ</span><sub><span>p</span></sub><span> = 0.4μ</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span>)</span></p><p><span>= (4.2 × 10</span><sup><span>19</span></sup><span>) / (1.5 × 10</span><sup><span>10 </span></sup><span>(1 + 0.4)) = 20,000</span></p>",
