        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>At T = 300 K, the band gap and the intrinsic carrier concentration of GaAs are 1.42 eV and 10</span><sup><span>6</span></sup><span> cm</span><sup><span>–3</span></sup><span> respectively. In order to generate electron hole pairs in GaAs, which one of the wavelength (λ</span><sub><span>c</span></sub><span>) ranges of incident radiation, is most suitable? (Given that: Plank’s constant is 6.62 ×10</span><sup><span>–34</span></sup><span> J-s, velocity of light is 3 ×10</span><sup><span>10</span></sup><span> cm/s and charge of electron is 1.6 ×10</span><sup><span>–19</span></sup><span> C )</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(GATE 2014 || EC || MCQ ||1 MARK)</strong></b></p>",
