        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tThe energy band diagram and the electron, density profile n (x) in a semiconductor are shown in the figures.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tAssume that n(x) = 10</span><sup><span>15</span></sup><span> cm</span><sup><span>–3</span></sup><span>, with  </span>[Tex]e^{\\frac{q \\alpha x}{kT}} \\, \\text{cm}^{-3}[/Tex]<span>= 0.1 V/cm </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\">[Tex]\\alpha[/Tex]<span> and x expressed in cm.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tGiven  </span>[Tex]\\frac{kT}{q}[/Tex]<span> = 0.026 V, D</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> = 36 cm</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span>s</span><sup><span>–1</span></sup><span>, and  </span>[Tex]\\frac{D}{\\mu} = \\frac{kT}{q}[/Tex]</p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"420851580\" height=\"528\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260504175027581410/420851580.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260504175027581410/420851580.webp 454w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260504175027581410/420851580-100.webp 86w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260504175027581410/420851580-200.webp 172w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260504175027581410/420851580-300.webp 258w\" width=\"454\"/><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><br/><b><strong>(GATE 2015 || EC || MCQ ||1 MARK)</strong></b></p>",
