        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t(1.55 to 1.65)</span><br/><span>We know that </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tNow C = </span><img height=\"37\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"21\"/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tWhere C = Capacitance </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tA = Area of a capacitor</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\tε = dielectric</span><br/><span>From the fig, C</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> and C</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> capacitors are in series/</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\tCeq = </span><img height=\"40\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"45\"/></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span> </span><img height=\"71\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"195\"/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\t= 2.5 × 10</span><sup><span>9</span></sup><span> ε</span><sub><span>0</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\tCeq = </span><img height=\"42\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"31\"/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\tt</span><sub><span>eq</span></sub><span> = </span><img height=\"42\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"67\"/><span>= </span><img height=\"42\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"67\"/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\t= 1.6 × 10</span><sup><span>–9</span></sup><span> m = 1.6 nm.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tSo, the value of thickness (t</span><sub><span>eq</span></sub><span>) is 1.6 nm.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
