        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>1.\tFlat band voltage is the voltage where there is a no-charge present in the oxide or oxide semiconductor interface.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>2.\tAs the gate voltage V</span><sub><span>G</span></sub><span> increase, more electrons are attracted to the oxide-semiconductor interface. A-n type channel is formed.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>-&gt; The inversion takes place at R</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>3. For negative gate voltage, more holes are accumulated near the gate.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>-&gt; Accumulations take place at P</span></p>",
