        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For M</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span>:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>V</span><sub><span>DS2</span></sub><span> ≥ V</span><sub><span>GS2</span></sub><span> − V</span><sub><span>TH</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Condition for saturation is satisfied, so M</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> is in saturation.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For M</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>V</span><sub><span>DS1</span></sub><span> &lt; V</span><sub><span>GS1</span></sub><span> − V</span><sub><span>TH</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So M</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> operates in linear region.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Hence, the states are:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Linear, Saturation</span></p>",
