        "id": 170432,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\tConsider an n-channel metal oxide semiconductor field effect transistor (MOSFET) with a gate-to-source voltage of 1.8V. Assume that  </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\">[Tex]\\frac{W}{L}[/Tex][Tex]\\frac{W}{L} = 4, \\quad \\mu_n C_{ox} = 70 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{ A/V}^2[/Tex]<span>, the threshold voltage is 0.3 V and the channel length modulation parameter is 0.09</span></p><img height=\"21\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"24\"/><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>. In the saturation region, the drain conductance (in micro Siemens) is   </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(GATE 2016 ||  EC || MCQ||1 MARK)</strong></b></p>",
