        "id": 170476,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>A solar cell of area 1.0 cm</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span>, operating at 1.0 sun intensity, has a short circuit current of 20 mA, and an open circuit voltage of 0.65 V. Assuming room temperature operation and thermal equivalent voltage of 26 mV, the open circuit voltage (in volts, correct to two decimal places) at 0.2 sun intensity is ___.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br><b><strong>(GATE 2018 || EC || NAT ||1 MARK)</strong></b></p>",
