        "id": 170482,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\tFor a particular intensity of incident light on a silicon pn junction solar cell, the photocurrent density (J</span><sub><span>L</span></sub><span>) is 2.5 mA/cm</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span> and the open-circuit voltage (V</span><sub><span>oc</span></sub><span>) is 0.451 V. Consider thermal voltage (V</span><sub><span>T</span></sub><span>) to be 25 mV. If the intensity of the incident light is increased by 20 times, assuming that the temperature remains unchanged, V</span><sub><span>oc</span></sub><span> (in volts) will be </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>( GATE 2007 || EC || NAT ||1 MARK)</strong></b></p>",
