        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t(0.99 to 1.01)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tFor the unity feedback and step input to a type-1 system, the steady-state error is zero. For ramp input, the steady-state error is finite, i.e. (1 / k</span><sub><span>v</span></sub><span>) and for parabolic input, the steady-state error is infinity.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tHence, the given system must be type-1 (p = 1).</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>",
