        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>N = P – Z</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tN = Number of encirclements of (–1 + j0). It is positive if Nyquist Plot encircles the point (–1 + j0) in the counterclockwise direction.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tZ = Number of closed-loop poles lying in the right half of s plane</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tP = Number of open-loop poles lying in the right half of s plane</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tFor stability, Z = 0</span></p>",
