        "id": 165462,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The Nyquist plot of a stable transfer function </span>[Tex]G(s)[/Tex]<span> is shown in the figure. We are interested in the stability of the closed-loop system in the feedback configuration shown below.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-12-103847\" height=\"140\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260512103908459028/Screenshot-2026-05-12-103847.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260512103908459028/Screenshot-2026-05-12-103847.png 355w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260512103908459028/Screenshot-2026-05-12-103847-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260512103908459028/Screenshot-2026-05-12-103847-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260512103908459028/Screenshot-2026-05-12-103847-300.png 300w\" width=\"355\"/><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The gain and phase margins of G(s) for closed-loop stability are</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>( GATE 2009 ||  EC || MCQ ||2 MARK)</strong></b><br/></p>",
