        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p>[Tex]G(s) = \\frac{1}{s(s^2 + s + 1)}[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]= \\frac{1}{\\omega\\sqrt{(1-\\omega^2)^2 + \\omega^2}}[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]\\phi = -90^\\circ - \\tan^{-1}\\left( \\frac{\\omega}{1 - \\omega^2} \\right)[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For phase-crossover frequency ω</span><sub><span>pc</span></sub><span>,</span></p><p>[Tex]\\angle G(s)H(s) = -180^\\circ[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]-90^\\circ - \\tan^{-1}(\\frac{\\omega}  {1 - \\omega^2}) = -180^\\circ[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]- \\tan^{-1}(\\frac{\\omega}  {1 - \\omega^2}) = -90^\\circ[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]\\frac{\\omega}{1-\\omega^2} = \\frac{1}{0}[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>1 – ω</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span> = 0</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>ω</span><sub><span>pc</span></sub><span> = ω = 1 rad/s</span></p><p>[Tex]\\left| G(s)H(s) \\right|_{\\omega=\\omega_{\\text{pc}}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(1-1^2)^2+1^2}} = 1[/Tex]</p>",
