        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>In a Bode magnitude plot:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>A slope change of −20 dB/dec indicates 1 pole.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>A slope change of +20 dB/dec indicates 1 zero.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Counting the slope changes at each corner frequency:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Poles: 2+1+2+1=6</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Zeros: 1+1+1=3</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Therefore, the system has:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>N</span><sub><span>p</span></sub><span>= 6, N</span><sub><span>z</span></sub><span>= 3</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So, the transfer function contains 6 poles and 3 zeros.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
