        "id": 165563,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>The figure below shows the Bode magnitude and phase plots of a stable transfer function</span></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t</span><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXf5dfWhkLlBQ-U7rGx9JKNuugxYBihzoEK7nLVi2lZhabni2WhWuM3-8EC8fyzdcOGO-u2Yx-ibeqF9BNZezaTbUvE3BJ5OsGscY9TdS0jJIhCQ12lV1VwO4UtGph4Y70mOa-oA3A?key=anOcZ8-Jg9pQ0dE-pHoJaQ\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" loading=\"auto\"></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250828110721166369/Screenshot-2025-08-28-110800.png\" alt=\"Screenshot-2025-08-28-110800\" width=\"557\" height=\"237\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250828110721166369/Screenshot-2025-08-28-110800.png 557w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250828110721166369/Screenshot-2025-08-28-110800-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250828110721166369/Screenshot-2025-08-28-110800-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250828110721166369/Screenshot-2025-08-28-110800-300.png 300w\" loading=\"auto\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>Consider the negative unity feedback configuration with gain k in the feedforward path. The closed-loop is stable for k&lt; k</span><sub><span>0</span></sub><span>. The maximum value of k</span><sub><span>0</span></sub><span> is</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>(GATE 2018 ||  EC || NAT ||2 MARK)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>",
