        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>Change in magnitude from 1 rad/s to 10 rad/s</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\t\t= 32 – (–8) = 40 dB.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span> </span>[Tex]\\text{Slope} = \\frac{\\text{Change in magnitude}}{\\text{Change in frequency}}[/Tex]</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span> </span>[Tex]= -\\frac{40}{1} = -40\\text{dB / decade}[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tAn initial slope of –40 dB/decade means there are two poles at the origin. It means either option (b) or option (d) is correct.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tGiven: |G(s) |</span><sub><span>ω=1</span></sub><span> rad/s = 32 dB.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tOption (b): </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\">[Tex]20 \\log \\left| \\frac{K}{(1)^2} \\right| = 32\\text{dB}[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tK=39.81</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
