        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>Let the state-space representation of an LT1 system be x’(t) = Ax (t) + Bu (t), y(t) = Cx(t) + du (t) where A, B, C are matrices, d is a scalar, u(t) is the input to the system, and y (t) is its output. Let B = [0 0 1]</span><sup><span>T</span></sup><span> and d = 0. Which one of the following options for A and C will ensure that the transfer function of this LTI system is </span>[Tex]H(s) = \\frac{1}{s^3 + 3s^2 + 2s + 1}[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(GATE 2019 || EC || MCQ|| 2 MARK)</strong></b></p>",
