        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>An emitter resistor provides negative feedback.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>If temperature increases, collector current tends to increase, but emitter resistor opposes this change.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>If transistor β\\betaβ changes, the emitter resistor also stabilizes the current.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So the operating point becomes stable against both effects.</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
