        "id": 165349,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The small-signal resistance (i.e., dV</span><sub><span>B</span></sub><span>/dI</span><sub><span>D</span></sub><span>) in kΩ offered by the n-channel MOSFET ‘M’ shown in the figure below, at a bias point of V</span><sub><span>B</span></sub><span> = 2V is (device data for M</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> device transconductance parameter k</span><sub><span>N</span></sub><span> = μ</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> C</span><sub><span>ox</span></sub><span> (W/L) = 40 μA/V</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span>, threshold voltage V</span><sub><span>TN</span></sub><span> = 1V, and neglect body effect and channel length modulation effects)</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2025-08-27-120157\" height=\"169\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250827120211550198/Screenshot-2025-08-27-120157.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250827120211550198/Screenshot-2025-08-27-120157.png 224w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250827120211550198/Screenshot-2025-08-27-120157-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250827120211550198/Screenshot-2025-08-27-120157-200.png 200w\" width=\"224\"/><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(GATE 2013 || EC || PYQ || MCQ || 2 MARKS)</strong></b></p>",
