        "id": 165365,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For the n-channel MOS transistor shown in the figure, the threshold voltage V</span><sub><span>th</span></sub><span> is 0.8 V. Neglect channel length modulation effects. When the drain voltage V</span><sub><span>D</span></sub><span> = 1.6 V, the drain current I</span><sub><span>D</span></sub><span> was found to be 0.5 mA. If V</span><sub><span>D</span></sub><span> is adjusted to be 2 V by changing the values of R and V</span><sub><span>DD</span></sub><span>, the new value of I</span><sub><span>D</span></sub><span> (in mA) is</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2025-08-27-121425\" height=\"203\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250827121437492614/Screenshot-2025-08-27-121425.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250827121437492614/Screenshot-2025-08-27-121425.png 294w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250827121437492614/Screenshot-2025-08-27-121425-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250827121437492614/Screenshot-2025-08-27-121425-200.png 200w\" width=\"294\"/><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>( GATE 2014 || EC || PYQ || MCQ || 2 MARKS)</strong></b></p>",
