        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>First op-amp is an inductor-feedback differentiator/integrator combination.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given:</span></p><p>[Tex]V_s = 10\\cos(100t)[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>At ω=100:</span></p><p>[Tex]X_L = \\omega L = 100 \\times 10mH = 1\\Omega[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Gain of first stage:</span></p><p>[Tex]\\frac{X_L}{R} = \\frac{1}{10} = 0.1[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Second stage is an integrator with:</span></p><p>[Tex]RC = 100 \\times 10\\mu F = 10^{-3}[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Overall transfer gives unity gain, so:</span></p><p>[Tex]V_o = 10\\cos(100t)[/Tex]</p>",
