        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let the driving point impedance of N is</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>N</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> = R</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> + jX</span><sub><span>1</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Re[Z</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>(jω)] = R</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>\t…(1)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Since, N is passive network so R</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> is positive.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Total impedance Z</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> is given by,</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Z</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> = R</span><sub><span>neg</span></sub><span> + Z</span><sub><span>1</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Z</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> = (R</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> + R</span><sub><span>neg</span></sub><span>) + jX</span><sub><span>1</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Z</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> will be positive real function.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>If Re[Z</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span>] = R</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> + R</span><sub><span>neg</span></sub><span> ≥ 0</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>R</span><sub><span>neg</span></sub><span> ≥ – R</span><sub><span>1</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>As R</span><sub><span>neg</span></sub><span> is the negative resistance,</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>|R</span><sub><span>neg</span></sub><span>| ≤ R</span><sub><span>1</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>From equation (1),</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>|R</span><sub><span>neg</span></sub><span>| ≤ Re [Z</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>(jω)]</span></p>",
