        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The voltage e</span><sub><span>o</span></sub><span> is across the middle 4Ω resistor.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>From the middle node to ground, there are two parallel paths:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>4Ω</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>2Ω+2Ω=4Ω</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So,</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>4Ω∥4Ω=2Ω</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Now the circuit becomes:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>4Ωin series with2Ω</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Total resistance:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>R</span><sub><span>T</span></sub><span>=4+2=6Ω</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Current:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>I = 12/6 = 2A</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Voltage across the parallel combination (which is e</span><sub><span>0</span></sub><span>):</span></p><p>[Tex]e_0=I\\times 2\\Omega=2\\times 2=4V[/Tex]</p>",
