        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given:</span></p><p>[Tex]V_1=20V[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Dependent current source value:</span></p><p>[Tex]I_s=\\frac{V_1}{5}=\\frac{20}{5}=4A[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let the top node voltage be V.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Applying KCL at the top node:</span></p><p>[Tex]\\frac{V-20}{5}+\\frac{V}{5}=4[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]2V-20=20[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]V=20V[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So the current through the dependent source is 4A upward, and the voltage across it is 20V (top terminal positive).</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Power: P=VI=20 x 4=80W</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Since the current enters the negative terminal of the current source, the source delivers power.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>P=80W</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
