        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tKVL gives,&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\t\t</span><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"102\" height=\"41\" loading=\"auto\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tOr\t20 = 5I + (4 + I) 5</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>I = 0 amp</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t∴ Power delivered = 4</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span> × 5 = 80 W</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t</span><b><strong>Alternative method</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tApplying KCL at the node</span></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\t\t</span><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"192\" height=\"41\" loading=\"auto\"><span>&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\t\t20 – V + 20 = V</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\t\t40 = 2V</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\t\tV = 20 V</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tPower = </span><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"48\" height=\"34\" loading=\"auto\"><span> = 20 × 4 = 80 W</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tAs current leaves the positive voltage terminal, it delivers power&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>",
