        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250906171155180338/Screenshot-2025-09-06-171205.png\" alt=\"Screenshot-2025-09-06-171205\" width=\"506\" height=\"351\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250906171155180338/Screenshot-2025-09-06-171205.png 506w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250906171155180338/Screenshot-2025-09-06-171205-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250906171155180338/Screenshot-2025-09-06-171205-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250906171155180338/Screenshot-2025-09-06-171205-300.png 300w\" loading=\"auto\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p><br><span>\t</span><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"101\" height=\"35\" loading=\"auto\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t\tV</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> = 5 Volt</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t\t⇒ V</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> – V</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> = 4 × 5 (Ohm’s law)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t\tV</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> = 25 V</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t</span><b><strong>Alternative Method</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\tApplying KCL at the upper node.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\tThe other 4Ω resistor will also have I current&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t\t5 = I + I + 2 I</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t5 = 4 I</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t\tI = </span><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"13\" height=\"35\" loading=\"auto\"><span> = 1.25 A</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t\tV</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> = 4 I = 4 × 1.25 = 5V</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\tApplying KVL in the left-most loop.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t\tV</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> – 4 × 5 – I × 4 = 0</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t\tV</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> = 4 × 5 + 1.25 × 4&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>\t\t\t\tV</span><sub><span>2 </span></sub><span>= 25 V</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>",
