        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For maximum power transfer in an AC network, the load impedance must be the complex conjugate of the source/output impedance.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>If the first section has output impedance Z</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>, then the input impedance of the second section should be:</span></p><p>[Tex]Z_2=Z_1^{*}[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>where ∗ denotes the complex conjugate.</span></p>",
