        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>We need the average (DC) value of V</span><sub><span>ab</span></sub></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Using superposition:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The AC source 5πsin(5000t) has zero average value.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>For the DC component:</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Capacitor acts as open circuit.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Inductor acts as short circuit.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Since the capacitor is open, no DC current flows. Therefore:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>No voltage drop across 1kΩ or 2kΩ.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Node b is at 0 V (left source has zero DC value).</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Node a is at +5 V (connected to the 5 V source through zero current).</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Hence,</span></p><p>[Tex]V_{ab}=V_a-V_b=5-0=5V[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]V_{ab,\\mathrm{avg}}=5V[/Tex]</p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
