        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Before t=0, the switch is closed for a long time, so the inductor acts as a short circuit.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Hence the 2.5 A source current flows through the inductor branch:</span></p><p>[Tex]i_L(0^-)=2.5A[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Inductor current cannot change instantaneously:</span></p><p>[Tex]i_L(0^+)=2.5A[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Just after opening the switch, this 2.5 A current flows through the 20 Ω resistor.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>V</span><sub><span>x </span></sub><span>= iR = 2.5 x 20 = 50V</span></p><p>[Tex]V_x(0^+)=50V[/Tex]</p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
