        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>When the switch is closed at t = 0, capacitor C</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> will/discharge, and C</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> will get charged since both C</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> and C</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> are ideal, and there is no resistance in the circuit charging and discharging time constant will be zero. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Thus current will exist like an impulse function.</span></p>",
