        "id": 170425,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The electric field on the surface of a perfect conductor is 2 V/m. The conductor is immersed in water with </span>[Tex]\\epsilon = 80 \\epsilon_0[/Tex]<span>. The surface charge density on the conductor is</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br/><b><strong>(GATE 2002||  EC || MCQ ||2 MARK)</strong></b></p>",
