        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given: </span>[Tex]E = 2\\text{ V/m}, \\epsilon = 80\\ \\epsilon_0[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The total electric field of a perfect conductor is given by only the normal component.</span></p><p>[Tex]E_n = \\frac{\\rho_s}{\\epsilon_0 \\cdot \\epsilon_r}[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]\\Rightarrow 2 = \\frac{\\rho_s}{80 \\times 8.85 \\times 10^{-12}}[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]\\rho_s = 1.41 \\times 10^{-9}\\text{ C/m}^2[/Tex]</p>",
