        "id": 171538,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The magnetic field along the propagation direction inside a rectangular waveguide with the cross-section shown in figure is</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>H z = 3cos(2.094 × 10 2 x) cos(2.618 × 10 2 y) cos(6.283 × 10 10 t – βz)</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250919182741244210/Annotation-2025-09-19-055718.png\" alt=\"Annotation-2025-09-19-055718\" width=\"362\" height=\"173\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250919182741244210/Annotation-2025-09-19-055718.png 362w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250919182741244210/Annotation-2025-09-19-055718-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250919182741244210/Annotation-2025-09-19-055718-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250919182741244210/Annotation-2025-09-19-055718-300.png 300w\" loading=\"auto\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><br><span>(GATE 2012|| EC || MCQ ||2 MARK)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>",
