        "id": 171681,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider a 300 Ω, quarter-wave long (at 1 GHz) transmission line as shown in the figure. It is connected to a 10 V, 50 Ω source at one end and is left open circuited at the other end. The magnitude of the voltage at the open circuit end of the line is</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Annotation-2025-09-20-032535\" height=\"107\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920155607594289/Annotation-2025-09-20-032535.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920155607594289/Annotation-2025-09-20-032535.png 292w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920155607594289/Annotation-2025-09-20-032535-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920155607594289/Annotation-2025-09-20-032535-200.png 200w\" width=\"292\"/><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>(GATE 2004|| EC || MCQ ||2 MARK)</span><br/></p>",
