        "correctAnswers": [
          3
        ],
        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given: </span>[Tex]h(t)=e^{\\alpha t}u(t)+e^{\\beta t}u(-t)\n[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For stability of an LTI system:</span></p><p>[Tex]\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}|h(t)|\\,dt&lt;\\infty[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>First term</strong></b></p><p>[Tex]e^{\\alpha t}u(t)[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>exists for t ≥ 0, so it must decay as t→∞.</span></p><p>[Tex]\\alpha&lt;0[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Second term</strong></b></p><p>[Tex]e^{\\beta t}u(-t)[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>exists for t ≤ 0, so it must decay as t→−∞.</span></p><p>[Tex]\\beta&gt;0[/Tex]</p><p>[Tex]\\text{\\(\\alpha\\) is negative and \\(\\beta\\) is positive}[/Tex]</p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
