        "id": 168116,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A discrete time linear shift-invariant system has an impulse response h[n] with h[0] = 1, h[1] = –1, h[2] = 2 and zero otherwise. The system is given an input sequence x[n] with x[0] = x[2] = 1 and zero otherwise. The number of nonzero samples  in the output sequence y[n], and the value of y[2] are, respectively</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(GATE 2008 || EC || PYQ || MCQ || 2 MARKS)</strong></b></p>",
