        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>To find the impulse response, apply the input:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>x[n] = δ[n]</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Then:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>For n &lt; 0, the interval (−∞,n] does not contain k = 0, so y[n] = 0</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>For n ≥ 0, the interval contains k = 0, where ∣δ[0]∣ = 1</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Hence,</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>y[n] = 1</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Therefore,</span></p><p>[Tex]h[n]=\n\\begin{cases}\n0, &amp; n&lt;0\\\\\n1, &amp; n\\ge 0\n\\end{cases}\n=u[n][/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>h[n] = u[n]</span></p>",
