        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>The Fourier series of a real periodic function has only</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>\tP. Cosine terms if it is even</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>\tQ. Sine terms if it is even</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>\tR. Cosine terms if it is odd\t</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>\tS. Sine terms if it is odd</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tWhich of the above statements are correct?</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(GATE 2009 || EC || PYQ || MCQ || 1 MARKS)</strong></b></p>",
