        "id": 168255,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A periodic signal x(t) has a trigonometric Fourier series expansion </span>[Tex]x(t)=a_0+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\left(a_n\\cos(n\\omega_0 t)+b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0 t)\\right)[/Tex]<span>. If x(t) = –x(–t) = –x(t – π/ω</span><sub><span>0</span></sub><span>), we can conclude that:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(GATE 2017 || EC || PYQ || MCQ ||1 MARKS)</strong></b></p>",
        "options": [
          "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span> a</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> are zero for all n and b</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> are zero for n even.</span></p>",
          "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>a</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> are zero for all n and b</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> are zero for n odd.</span></p>",
          "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>a</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> are zero for n even and b</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> are zero for n odd.</span></p>",
          "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span> a</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> are zero for n odd and b</span><sub><span>n</span></sub><span> are zero for n even.</span></p>"
        ],
        "correctAnswer": 0,
