        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Let x(t) = 2 cos (800πt) + cos (1400 πt). x(t) is sampled with the rectangular pulse train shown in figure. The only spectral components (in kHz) present in the sampled signal in the frequency range 2.5 kHz to 3.5 kHz are</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2025-09-13-103424\" height=\"225\" loading=\"auto\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250913103434839442/Screenshot-2025-09-13-103424.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250913103434839442/Screenshot-2025-09-13-103424.png 396w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250913103434839442/Screenshot-2025-09-13-103424-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250913103434839442/Screenshot-2025-09-13-103424-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250913103434839442/Screenshot-2025-09-13-103424-300.png 300w\" width=\"396\"/><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(GATE 2003 || EC || NAT || 2 MARKS)</strong></b></p>",
