        "id": 169795,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A continuous time function x(t) is periodic with period T. The function is sampled uniformly with a sapling period T</span><sub><span>s</span></sub><span>. In which one of the following cases is the sampled signal periodic?</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(GATE 2016 || EC || MCQ || 1 MARK)</strong></b></p>",
        "options": [
          "<p>[Tex]T=\\sqrt{2}\\,T_s[/Tex]</p>",
          "<p>[Tex]T=1.2\\,T_s[/Tex]</p>",
          "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Always </span></p>",
          "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Never</span></p>"
        ],
        "correctAnswer": 1,
        "correctAnswers": [
          1
        ],
        "questionType": "MCQ",
        "natRange": null,
        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A signal is periodic if </span>[Tex]\\frac{T}{T_s}[/Tex]<span> is a rational number. For T = 1.2T</span><sub><span>s </span></sub><span> </span></p><p>[Tex]\\frac{T}{T_s}=1.2=\\frac{6}{5}[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Since </span>[Tex]\\frac{6}{5}[/Tex]<span>​ is a rational number, the signal is periodic. ​</span></p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
