        "id": 173542,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>Consider the following statements about the linear dependence of the real valued functions y</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> = 1, y</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> = x and y</span><sub><span>3</span></sub><span> = x</span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span>, over the field of real numbers.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tI. y</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>, y</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> and y</span><sub><span>3</span></sub><span> are linearly independent on –1 ≤ x ≤ 0.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tII. y</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>, y</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> and y</span><sub><span>3</span></sub><span> are linearly dependent on 0 ≤ x ≤ 1.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tIII. y</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>, y</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> and y</span><sub><span>3</span></sub><span> are linearly independent on 0 ≤ x ≤ 1.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tIV. y</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span>, y</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span> and y</span><sub><span>3</span></sub><span> are linearly dependent on –1 ≤ x ≤ 0.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tWhich one among the following is correct?</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>",
