        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>From the question, the complex variable function is:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t\tf(z) = 2z</span><sup><span>3</span></sup><span> + b</span><sub><span>1</span></sub><span> |z|</span><sup><span>3</span></sup></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tGiven f(z) is analytic.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\twhich is possible only when b = 0</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tsince |z</span><sup><span>3</span></sup><span>| is differentiable at the origin but not analytic.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\t2z</span><sup><span>3</span></sup><span> is analytic everywhere</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tf(z) = 2z</span><sup><span>3</span></sup><span> + b |z</span><sup><span>3</span></sup><span>| is analytic</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>\tonly when b = 0</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p>",
