        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider the following Amplitude Modulated (AM) signal, where f </span><sub><span>m</span></sub><span> &lt; B </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>x </span><sub><span>AM </span></sub><span>(t) = 10(1 + 0.5sin2 π f </span><sub><span>m</span></sub><span> t) cos2πf </span><sub><span>c</span></sub><span> t</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The AM signal gets added to a noise with Power Spectral Density S </span><sub><span>n </span></sub><span>(f) given in the figure below. The ratio of average sideband power to mean noise power would be</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250930135604813236/Screenshot-2025-09-30-012655.png\" alt=\"Screenshot-2025-09-30-012655\" width=\"342\" height=\"145\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250930135604813236/Screenshot-2025-09-30-012655.png 342w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250930135604813236/Screenshot-2025-09-30-012655-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250930135604813236/Screenshot-2025-09-30-012655-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250930135604813236/Screenshot-2025-09-30-012655-300.png 300w\" loading=\"auto\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>(PYQ || 2006 MCQ|| 2 MARK)</span><br></p>",
