        "explanation": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>An SSB (Single Sideband) signal contains only one sideband.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For:</span></p><p>[Tex]m(t) = \\cos(2\\pi f_m t)[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>DSB-SC gives frequencies at:</span></p><p>[Tex]f_c + f_m\n\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\nf_c - f_m[/Tex]</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>SSB keeps only one of them.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>So the Upper Sideband (USB) signal is:</span></p><p>[Tex]\\cos\\!\\left[2\\pi(f_c + f_m)t\\right][/Tex]</p>",
        "tag": "GATE ECE || MCQ"
