        "id": 172547,
        "question": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A source alphabet consists of N symbols with the probability of the first two symbols being the same. A source encoder increases the probability of the first symbol by a small amount  and decreases that of the second by ε. After encoding, the entropy of the source</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>(PYQ || 2012 MCQ || 1 MARK)</strong></b></p>",
